      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and many references say 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of serious toxicity, including lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg three times daily**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you intend, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest adding a note with the clinical rationale."
      }
     ],
