       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose twice the maximum. At 5,100 mg/day, the patient could be harmed, with a real risk of severe lactic acidosis.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose if the patient is new to metformin. A lower start is usually better tolerated.\n- **Enter the order with a note for pharmacy review.** If you have a clinical rationale I'm not aware of, I can add it to the note. The order would still need to be at or below the maximum dose, or go through your institution's process for exceeding it.\n\nIf you really need a dose above the maximum, I'd suggest talking with the pharmacist or the attending first. I'm happy to enter whichever of these you choose."
